--- mirror brief (secondmate home) delivery lines:
21:1. Push only your `fm/jt-task` work, only to `origin`, and only under a delivery name that does not exist there yet (`fm/jt-task`, then `fm/jt-task-r2`, `fm/jt-task-r3`, ... after a rebase). Never force-push in any form, never push to an existing branch, never open a PR, and never merge. The main firstmate lands the branch you report.
59:Delivery contract: mode=local-only
60:This task ships **local-only** from a local-origin mirror: no PR, no pipeline, and the only remote is `origin`, the project's authoritative working repository.
61:The task is complete only when committed on your branch `fm/jt-task` and that branch is pushed to `origin` with `git push origin fm/jt-task`. Push nothing else anywhere, do NOT open a PR, and do NOT merge.
62:Never force-push, in any form: no `--force`, no `--force-with-lease`, no `+` refspec, and never delete a branch in `origin`. A branch name you have pushed is never pushed to again.
63:Touch `origin` only through `git fetch`, `git ls-remote`, and those pushes: never read, copy, or write the files of the repository it points at.
64:Keep your work a clean fast-forward onto `origin`'s default branch. If that branch has advanced after you pushed, fetch, rebase your local `fm/jt-task` onto it, and push the result under the next unused delivery name instead: `git push origin fm/jt-task:refs/heads/fm/jt-task-r2`, then `fm/jt-task-r3`, and so on. Check `git ls-remote --heads origin 'fm/jt-task*'` first so the name you pick does not exist yet.
65:When it is implemented, committed, and pushed, append `done: ready in branch <exact branch name you last pushed> pushed to origin` to the status file (for example `done: ready in branch fm/jt-task pushed to origin`, or `fm/jt-task-r2` after one rebase) and stop.
